Vendored reference code and data for the `scmo_covid_sweden` benchmark.

  reference.R            mlsynth's runner: the numeric core of the authors'
                         COVID_analysis.R (fn_W synthetic-control QP via
                         quadprog::solve.QP, the three domains, the permutation
                         test, the aggregate index and the six robustness
                         variants), with every plotting call removed and the
                         objects the plots were drawn from printed instead.
                         Produces the captured bundle.
  COVID_analysis_orig.R  The authors' original script, vendored verbatim for
                         provenance (reference.R reproduces its computation).
  covid_panel.csv        The authors' assembled COVID panel (their
                         Data_COVID/data.csv), cut to the 27 countries, the
                         window 2019-01-01 to 2020-09-30, and the twelve
                         outcomes the three domains use. Written from
                         basedata/tlp_covid_sweden.parquet, which the Python
                         case reads, so both sides see the same numbers.

Source
  Tian, Wei, Seojeong Lee & Valentyn Panchenko (2026), "Synthetic Control with
  Multiple Outcomes," Econometrics Journal, Online Appendix B.3. Files taken
  from the authors' replication package (COVID_analysis.R, Data_COVID/).
  Vendored so the reference run is reproducible offline; all credit to the
  authors. These files produce the captured reference bundle only and are not
  part of the mlsynth library.
